course: dictionary
lesson: 4549
title: Heaters: warm and safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A heater is a machine that makes a room, a car, water or something else warm. Many heaters use electricity, gas or oil to make the heat.
explain: Heaters keep homes warm in winter, but they can be dangerous. «Never use a stove, heater or barbecue inside a tent», because fire can start and smoke can make you ill.
explain: Heat moves from the heater into the air and into things nearby. That is why clothes and curtains must be kept away from a heater: they can catch fire.
fact: A heater is a machine that makes things warm.
fact: Heaters can run on electricity, gas or oil.
fact: Carbon monoxide is a poison gas with no colour and no smell, so homes with fuel-burning heaters need a carbon monoxide alarm.
fact: Never cover a heater, and keep clothes, curtains and paper away from it. A boy in Leeds put a towel over a heater to dry it, and it started to burn.
fact: Electric heaters must never be near a bath or sink of water.
exercise: What is a heater? | *A machine that makes a room, a car or water warm | A tool for cutting paper | A cold box that keeps food fresh | A kind of bath
exercise: A boy in Leeds put a towel over a heater. Why was this dangerous? | The towel would make the room too bright | The towel would turn into water | The towel would get too cold | *The towel could catch fire
exercise: Which of these should be kept away from a heater? | *Clothes, curtains and paper | A cup of cold milk | Your pencil case in a drawer | Your school bag on the table
test: Why is carbon monoxide dangerous? | It has a sweet smell | It makes the room colder | *It is a poison gas you cannot see or smell | It is a kind of heater
test: Where must electric heaters never be? | Inside a book | In the garden | On the sofa | *Near a bath or sink of water
exam: Which is the safest thing to do with a heater? | Touch it while it is hot to check it | Use it inside a tent to keep warm | *Keep clothes and curtains away from it and never cover it | Cover it with a towel to dry socks
